WEBVTT

00:00:19.358 --> 00:00:21.377
Dad's missing I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:21.412 --> 00:00:22.605
I can't do this alone.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.046
Dad's giving us a job to do.

00:00:24.081 --> 00:00:26.071
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:26.106 --> 00:00:28.027
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:31.020
This Demon killed mom and
Jess. I got to find dad.

00:00:31.055 --> 00:00:32.768
I've got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:32.803 --> 00:00:33.601
I'm Meg.

00:00:33.636 --> 00:00:34.628
So, where are you headed?

00:00:34.663 --> 00:00:35.620
No way I'm telling you.

00:00:35.621 --> 00:00:37.985
You could be some freak.

00:00:38.532 --> 00:00:39.805
Dad.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.764
<i>ust to get a glimpse
beyond this illusion</i>

00:00:43.799 --> 00:00:44.981
<i>I was soaring ever</i>

00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:47.857
1835, Samuel Colt made a special gun.

00:00:47.892 --> 00:00:50.698
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:51.736 --> 00:00:55.422
<i>Though my eyes could see
I still was a blind man</i>

00:00:55.457 --> 00:00:59.108
<i>Though my mind could
think I still was a mad man</i>

00:00:59.143 --> 00:01:01.881
<i>I hear the voices when I'm dreaming</i>

00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:05.244
I have nightmares. And
sometime they come true.

00:01:07.106 --> 00:01:10.502
<i>Carry on my wayward son</i>

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.497
<i>There'll be peace when you are</i>

00:01:12.532 --> 00:01:15.668
You two are all I've got. But I
guess we are stronger as a family.

00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:17.642
We go after this thing, together.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.145
Yes, sir.

00:01:18.146 --> 00:01:20.703
<i>Don't you cry no more</i>

00:01:45.641 --> 00:01:46.920
Good morning.

00:01:47.611 --> 00:01:49.274
Can I help you?

00:01:50.413 --> 00:01:52.390
I kind of...

00:01:52.425 --> 00:01:54.367
I need to talk.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.363
That's what I'm here for.

00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:03.431
I've done some things.

00:02:04.664 --> 00:02:06.330
Not good things.

00:02:06.365 --> 00:02:09.169
Well, there's always
forgiveness for us who seek it.

00:02:09.204 --> 00:02:11.351
For everyone?

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.661
Are you sure?

00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:15.409
I'll like to say...

00:02:15.444 --> 00:02:18.911
Salvation was created for sinners.

00:02:20.348 --> 00:02:23.402
Tell me what's on your mind.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.081
Well, I've lied a lot.

00:02:28.116 --> 00:02:30.156
I've Stolen.

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:32.161
I've lusted...

00:02:32.196 --> 00:02:35.001
And the other day I met this man.

00:02:35.036 --> 00:02:38.744
A nice guy, you know?

00:02:39.465 --> 00:02:45.448
We had a really good
chat. Sort of like this.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.237
And I slit his throat and ripped
his heart out through his chest.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.281
Does that make me a bad person?

00:02:54.316 --> 00:02:55.837
I know what you are.

00:02:57.965 --> 00:03:00.268
You can't be here.

00:03:00.303 --> 00:03:02.025
This is hollowed ground.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.534
Please...

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:06.721
Maybe that works in the minor leagues.

00:03:06.756 --> 00:03:09.399
But not with me.

00:03:34.057 --> 00:03:36.655
You throw like a girl.

00:03:37.478 --> 00:03:39.698
What do you want?

00:03:40.146 --> 00:03:42.825
The Winchesters.

00:03:42.992 --> 00:03:46.431
I haven't spoken to John
Winchester for over a year.

00:03:46.466 --> 00:03:48.475
You're wasting you time.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.528
Even if I knew where they were

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.947
I'd never tell you.

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:55.072
I know.

00:04:45.777 --> 00:04:47.334
So, this is it?

00:04:47.369 --> 00:04:49.637
This is everything I know.

00:04:49.672 --> 00:04:52.569
Look, our whole lives we've been
searching for this demon right?

00:04:52.604 --> 00:04:54.962
Not a trace. Just nothing.

00:04:54.997 --> 00:04:57.286
Until about a year ago.

00:04:57.321 --> 00:04:59.452
For the first time I picked up a trail.

00:04:59.487 --> 00:05:00.649
That's when you took off.

00:05:00.684 --> 00:05:01.586
Yeah.

00:05:01.621 --> 00:05:05.354
The demon must have come
out of hiding or hibernation.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.567
All right, so what's
this trail you've found?

00:05:07.602 --> 00:05:11.067
Starts in Arizona. Then
New Jersey, California.

00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:13.423
House is burned down to the ground.

00:05:13.458 --> 00:05:16.110
It's going after families.

00:05:16.145 --> 00:05:17.696
Just like it went after us.

00:05:17.731 --> 00:05:19.115
Families with infants?

00:05:19.116 --> 00:05:20.136
Yeah.

00:05:20.171 --> 00:05:23.220
The night of the kid's
six month birthday.

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:25.325
I was six months old that night?

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.965
Exactly six months.

00:05:27.019 --> 00:05:32.416
So, basically this demon is going
after these kids for some reason.

00:05:33.148 --> 00:05:35.852
Same way it came for me.

00:05:36.597 --> 00:05:39.587
So, mom's death?

00:05:39.874 --> 00:05:41.440
Jessica, it's all because of me?

00:05:41.475 --> 00:05:42.342
We don't know that Sam.

00:05:42.343 --> 00:05:43.955
Oh, really? Cause I say
we're pretty damn sure Dean.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.413
For the last time. What happened
to them is not your fault.

00:05:46.448 --> 00:05:48.837
Yeah, you're right. It's not
my fault. But it's my problem.

00:05:48.872 --> 00:05:50.837
No, it's not your
problem. It's our problem.

00:05:50.872 --> 00:05:54.908
Okay. That's enough.

00:06:00.068 --> 00:06:01.862
So, why is it doing it?

00:06:01.897 --> 00:06:02.948
What does it want?

00:06:02.983 --> 00:06:05.701
I wish I had more answers. I do.

00:06:05.736 --> 00:06:08.385
I've always been one step behind it.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:12.060
Look I've never got
there in time to save...

00:06:17.248 --> 00:06:20.479
So how do we find it?
Before it hits again?

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:22.647
There' re signs.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.214
Look, it took me a
while to see the patterns

00:06:24.249 --> 00:06:29.135
but days before these fires
signs crop up in an area.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:34.022
Cattle deaths, temperature
fluctuations, electrical storms.

00:06:34.577 --> 00:06:37.581
And then we backed and checked...

00:06:37.616 --> 00:06:40.887
These things happened in Lawrence?

00:06:40.922 --> 00:06:44.158
A week before your mother died.

00:06:46.041 --> 00:06:48.987
And in Palo Alto.

00:06:50.881 --> 00:06:53.308
Before Jessica.

00:06:53.343 --> 00:06:57.702
And these signs they're starting again.

00:06:58.086 --> 00:07:00.194
Where?

00:07:00.332 --> 00:07:03.325
Salvation, Iowa.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.385
Damn it!

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.416
What is it?

00:07:37.451 --> 00:07:38.571
Son of a bitch!

00:07:38.606 --> 00:07:39.692
What is it?

00:07:40.145 --> 00:07:41.676
I just got a call from Caleb.

00:07:41.711 --> 00:07:42.962
Is he okay?

00:07:42.997 --> 00:07:46.198
He's fine. Jim Murphy's dead.

00:07:46.233 --> 00:07:48.291
Pastor Jim?

00:07:49.342 --> 00:07:51.343
How?

00:07:51.378 --> 00:07:53.442
Throat was slashed.

00:07:53.477 --> 00:07:56.157
He bled out.

00:07:58.989 --> 00:08:02.009
Caleb said they found traces
of sulfur at Jim's place.

00:08:02.044 --> 00:08:03.620
The Demon?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.971
The Demon?

00:08:06.006 --> 00:08:08.978
I don't know. Could be. He just got...

00:08:09.013 --> 00:08:12.075
He got careless he slipped up.

00:08:12.868 --> 00:08:16.287
Maybe the Demon knows
we're getting close.

00:08:16.322 --> 00:08:17.518
What do you want to do?

00:08:17.553 --> 00:08:19.886
Now we act like every second counts.

00:08:19.921 --> 00:08:22.995
There's two hospitals and a
health center in this County.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:25.053
We split up, we cover more ground.

00:08:25.088 --> 00:08:26.423
I want records.

00:08:26.458 --> 00:08:30.525
I want a list of every infant who's
gonna be six months old in the next week.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.521
Dad, that can be dozens of kids.

00:08:32.556 --> 00:08:34.410
How the hell are we gonna
know which one's the right one?

00:08:34.445 --> 00:08:37.051
We check them all. That's how.

00:08:37.543 --> 00:08:40.298
You got any better ideas?

00:08:41.822 --> 00:08:43.752
No, sir.

00:08:52.522 --> 00:08:53.939
Dad?

00:08:57.064 --> 00:08:59.123
Yeah.

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:02.739
It's Jim.

00:09:03.113 --> 00:09:05.406
You know, I can't...

00:09:11.474 --> 00:09:13.638
This ends, now.

00:09:13.673 --> 00:09:15.767
I'm ending it.

00:09:15.802 --> 00:09:18.802
I don't care what it takes.

00:10:08.493 --> 00:10:09.704
Here you go, officer.

00:10:09.739 --> 00:10:10.853
Thank you.

00:10:26.957 --> 00:10:30.075
Hi, is there anything I can do for you?

00:10:30.434 --> 00:10:32.800
Oh, God, yes.

00:10:34.484 --> 00:10:37.092
Only I uh...

00:10:37.127 --> 00:10:40.044
Working right now, so...

00:11:30.237 --> 00:11:32.364
Train.

00:12:40.892 --> 00:12:42.175
Hi.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:46.015
Here, let me hold that. I don't
think you need that anymore.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.666
She's gorgeous, is she yours?

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:49.333
Yeah.

00:12:49.368 --> 00:12:50.863
Oh, wow. Hi.

00:12:50.864 --> 00:12:53.832
I'm sorry, I'm Sam. I
just moved in up the block.

00:12:53.867 --> 00:12:55.291
Oh, hey. I'm Monica.

00:12:55.326 --> 00:12:55.760
Monica.

00:12:55.761 --> 00:12:56.684
This is Rosy.

00:12:56.719 --> 00:12:57.277
Rosy?

00:12:57.278 --> 00:12:59.702
Yeah. So, welcome to the neighborhood.

00:12:59.737 --> 00:13:01.242
Thank you.

00:13:01.277 --> 00:13:02.800
She's such a good baby.

00:13:02.835 --> 00:13:04.989
I know, she... I mean, she never cries.

00:13:05.024 --> 00:13:07.197
She just stares at everybody.

00:13:07.232 --> 00:13:09.336
Sometimes she looks at you and...

00:13:09.371 --> 00:13:12.206
I swear it's like
she's reading your mind.

00:13:12.414 --> 00:13:14.873
What about you Monica?
Have you lived here long?

00:13:14.908 --> 00:13:17.914
Oh, my husband and I we bought this
place just before Rosy was born.

00:13:17.949 --> 00:13:19.159
How old is Rosy?

00:13:19.194 --> 00:13:21.108
She's six months today.

00:13:22.273 --> 00:13:25.412
It's big right? Growing like a weed.

00:13:25.447 --> 00:13:27.182
Yeah.

00:13:31.618 --> 00:13:33.624
Monica...

00:13:33.985 --> 00:13:35.750
Yeah?

00:13:37.713 --> 00:13:39.087
Just uh...

00:13:39.122 --> 00:13:40.892
Just take care of yourself, okay?

00:13:40.927 --> 00:13:43.225
Yeah, you too Sam. We'll see you around.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:43.744
Yeah.

00:13:45.479 --> 00:13:48.077
Oh, here's daddy!

00:14:52.728 --> 00:14:54.453
What are you...?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.760
Rosy?

00:15:11.613 --> 00:15:13.525
No!

00:15:25.364 --> 00:15:27.333
A vision?

00:15:27.368 --> 00:15:29.289
Yes.

00:15:29.481 --> 00:15:32.640
I saw the Demon burning
a woman on the ceiling.

00:15:32.675 --> 00:15:35.107
Right and you think this is gonna
happen to this woman you met because...

00:15:35.142 --> 00:15:38.991
Because these things happen
exactly the way I see them.

00:15:39.026 --> 00:15:40.914
He started them as nightmares and...

00:15:40.949 --> 00:15:43.138
It started when he was awake.

00:15:43.173 --> 00:15:44.970
Yeah.

00:15:45.383 --> 00:15:48.592
It's like... I don't know,
it's like the closer I get...

00:15:48.627 --> 00:15:51.951
To anything involving the Demon
the stronger the visions get.

00:15:51.986 --> 00:15:55.045
All right, when were you
gonna tell me about this?

00:15:56.173 --> 00:15:57.592
We didn't know what it meant.

00:15:57.627 --> 00:16:02.665
All right, something like this starts happening to
your brother you pick up the phone and you call me.

00:16:03.111 --> 00:16:05.002
Call you?

00:16:05.791 --> 00:16:08.016
Are you kidding me?

00:16:08.808 --> 00:16:10.893
Dad, I called you from Lawrence.

00:16:10.928 --> 00:16:13.677
All right, Sam called
you when I was dying.

00:16:13.732 --> 00:16:17.193
I mean, getting you on the phone I got
a better chance winning the lottery.

00:16:22.548 --> 00:16:24.809
You're right.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:31.420
Although, I'm not crazy about this new
tone of yours, you're right. I'm sorry.

00:16:31.455 --> 00:16:32.875
Look, guys. Visions or no visions.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:36.055
The fact is we know the
Demon is coming tonight.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:39.195
And this family is going through
the same hell that we went through.

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.864
No, they're not.

00:16:40.899 --> 00:16:44.260
No one is. Ever again.

00:16:50.663 --> 00:16:52.318
Hello.

00:16:52.353 --> 00:16:53.973
Sam?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.603
Who is this?

00:16:55.638 --> 00:16:59.784
Think real hard, it'll come to you.

00:17:00.647 --> 00:17:02.478
Meg?

00:17:04.778 --> 00:17:07.061
Last time I saw you,
you fell out of a window.

00:17:07.096 --> 00:17:09.044
Yeah, thanks to you.

00:17:09.079 --> 00:17:11.400
That really hurt my feelings by the way.

00:17:11.435 --> 00:17:13.116
Just your feelings?

00:17:13.151 --> 00:17:15.719
That was a seven story drop.

00:17:15.754 --> 00:17:18.287
Let me speak to your dad.

00:17:20.763 --> 00:17:22.262
My dad?

00:17:22.297 --> 00:17:23.643
I don't know where my dad is.

00:17:23.678 --> 00:17:29.442
It's time for the grown ups to
talk, Sam. Let me speak to him, now.

00:17:38.112 --> 00:17:39.954
This is John.

00:17:39.989 --> 00:17:42.425
Howdy, John? I'm Meg.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.827
I'm a friend of your boys.

00:17:44.862 --> 00:17:48.518
I'm also the one who watched Jim
Murphy choke on his own blood.

00:17:51.185 --> 00:17:53.608
Still there, John boy?

00:17:53.643 --> 00:17:54.805
I'm here.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.532
That was yesterday.

00:17:56.533 --> 00:17:59.118
Today I'm in Lincoln.

00:18:00.874 --> 00:18:04.160
Visiting another old friend of yours.

00:18:04.195 --> 00:18:07.175
He wants to say hi.

00:18:07.501 --> 00:18:09.315
John, whatever they do don't...

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.871
Caleb?

00:18:12.088 --> 00:18:14.049
Caleb?

00:18:14.479 --> 00:18:16.143
You listen to me...

00:18:16.178 --> 00:18:19.512
He's got nothing to do with
anything. You let him go.

00:18:19.547 --> 00:18:22.646
We know you have the Colt, John.

00:18:22.988 --> 00:18:25.016
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:25.051 --> 00:18:26.732
Oh?

00:18:26.767 --> 00:18:28.414
Okay.

00:18:29.016 --> 00:18:31.581
So, listen to this.

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.263
Caleb?

00:18:37.446 --> 00:18:38.509
Caleb?

00:18:38.544 --> 00:18:40.000
You hear that?

00:18:40.035 --> 00:18:41.842
That's the sound of your friend dying.

00:18:41.877 --> 00:18:43.961
Now, let's try this again.

00:18:43.996 --> 00:18:47.295
We know you have the gun,
John. Words travel fast.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:51.367
So as far as we're concerned,
you just declared war.

00:18:51.402 --> 00:18:55.404
And this is what war looks
like. It has casualties.

00:18:56.243 --> 00:18:58.924
I'm gonna kill you, you know that?

00:18:58.959 --> 00:19:00.735
Oh, John. Please.

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:02.509
Mind your blood pressure.

00:19:02.544 --> 00:19:04.214
So, this is the thing.

00:19:04.249 --> 00:19:06.927
We're gonna keep doing what we're doing.

00:19:06.962 --> 00:19:08.680
And your friends...

00:19:08.715 --> 00:19:10.644
and anyone who has ever helped you?

00:19:10.679 --> 00:19:15.052
Gave you shelter, anyone you ever loved.

00:19:15.087 --> 00:19:19.426
They'll all die unless
you give us that gun.

00:19:23.119 --> 00:19:28.180
I'm waiting Johny. Better
answer before the buzzer.

00:19:28.633 --> 00:19:30.108
Okay.

00:19:30.143 --> 00:19:33.702
Sorry? I didn't quite get that.

00:19:33.737 --> 00:19:35.380
I said okay.

00:19:35.415 --> 00:19:37.915
I'll bring you the Colt.

00:19:38.246 --> 00:19:40.216
There's a warehouse in Lincoln.

00:19:40.251 --> 00:19:42.726
In the corner of Wellbasher and Lake.

00:19:42.761 --> 00:19:44.531
You're gonna meet me there.

00:19:44.566 --> 00:19:47.233
It's gonna take me about
a day's drive to get there.

00:19:47.268 --> 00:19:49.294
Meet me there at midnight tonight.

00:19:49.329 --> 00:19:50.033
That's impossible.

00:19:50.034 --> 00:19:52.995
I can't get there in time and I
can't just carry a gun on a plane.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:57.007
Oh, then I guess your
friends die, don't they?

00:19:58.005 --> 00:20:00.114
If you do decide to make it...

00:20:00.149 --> 00:20:02.343
Come alone.

00:20:09.541 --> 00:20:12.889
What the hell are you looking at?

00:20:13.341 --> 00:20:15.534
So you think Meg is a demon?

00:20:15.569 --> 00:20:18.163
Either that or she's possessed by one.

00:20:18.198 --> 00:20:19.338
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:19.481 --> 00:20:19.481
What do we do?

00:20:19.516 --> 00:20:21.436
I'm going to Lincoln.

00:20:21.471 --> 00:20:22.353
What?

00:20:22.354 --> 00:20:24.231
Doesn't seem like I have a choice.

00:20:24.266 --> 00:20:27.856
If I don't go, a lot of
people die. Our friends die.

00:20:27.891 --> 00:20:30.133
Dad, the Demon is coming tonight.

00:20:30.168 --> 00:20:32.433
For Monica and her family
that gun is all we've got.

00:20:32.468 --> 00:20:34.238
You can't just hand it over.

00:20:34.273 --> 00:20:36.008
Who said about handing it over?

00:20:36.009 --> 00:20:38.878
Look, besides us and a couple of
vampires no one's really seen the gun.

00:20:38.913 --> 00:20:40.401
No one knows what it looks like.

00:20:40.436 --> 00:20:43.297
So what? You're just gonna
pick up a ringer in a pawn shop?

00:20:43.332 --> 00:20:45.779
Antique store.

00:20:45.987 --> 00:20:48.345
You're gonna hand Meg a fake
gun and hopes she doesn't notice?

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:50.435
Look, as long as it's close...

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:52.169
She shouldn't be able
to tell the difference.

00:20:52.204 --> 00:20:54.922
Yeah, but for how long? What
happens when she figures it out?

00:20:54.957 --> 00:20:56.144
I just...

00:20:56.179 --> 00:20:59.333
I just need to buy a
few hours, that's all.

00:20:59.368 --> 00:21:02.512
You mean for Dean and me?

00:21:04.971 --> 00:21:08.783
You want us to stay here?

00:21:09.451 --> 00:21:11.732
And kill this Demon by ourselves.

00:21:11.767 --> 00:21:14.065
No, Sam.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:16.843
I want to stop losing people we love.

00:21:16.878 --> 00:21:21.608
I want you to go to school I
want... I want Dean to have a home.

00:21:26.109 --> 00:21:29.790
I want Mary alive.

00:21:32.724 --> 00:21:34.831
It's just...

00:21:37.137 --> 00:21:41.046
I just want this to be over.

00:22:13.014 --> 00:22:14.847
Did you get it?

00:22:27.533 --> 00:22:30.168
You know this is a trap, don't you?

00:22:32.104 --> 00:22:33.843
That's why Meg wanted you to come alone.

00:22:33.878 --> 00:22:35.297
I can handle her.

00:22:35.332 --> 00:22:38.311
I have the wholed loaded.
Holy water, mandake, amu...

00:22:38.346 --> 00:22:39.807
Dad.

00:22:39.842 --> 00:22:41.269
What?

00:22:41.765 --> 00:22:43.384
Promise me something.

00:22:43.419 --> 00:22:45.509
What's that?

00:22:45.686 --> 00:22:49.726
If this doesn't go south
just get the hell out.

00:22:49.761 --> 00:22:54.034
Don't get yourself killed, all
right? You're no good to us dead.

00:22:56.741 --> 00:22:59.621
Same goes for you.

00:23:00.697 --> 00:23:03.066
All right, listen to me.

00:23:03.832 --> 00:23:07.409
They made the bullets
special for this Colt.

00:23:07.444 --> 00:23:09.697
Only four of them left.

00:23:09.732 --> 00:23:13.374
Without them, this gun is useless.

00:23:15.059 --> 00:23:17.149
You make every shot count.

00:23:17.184 --> 00:23:18.664
Yes, sir.

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:24.703
I've been waiting a
long time for this fight.

00:23:24.738 --> 00:23:28.956
Now it's here and I'm
not gonna be in it.

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:32.884
It's up to you boys now.

00:23:34.794 --> 00:23:37.339
It's your fight. You finish this.

00:23:37.374 --> 00:23:39.523
You finished what I started.

00:23:39.558 --> 00:23:41.919
You understand?

00:24:02.362 --> 00:24:05.059
We'll see you soon dad.

00:24:09.208 --> 00:24:10.905
I'll see you later.

00:24:35.883 --> 00:24:37.918
Later...

00:26:00.743 --> 00:26:02.894
Maybe we can tell them
there's a gas leak.

00:26:02.929 --> 00:26:05.577
Might get them out of
the house for a few hours.

00:26:05.612 --> 00:26:09.136
How many times did that work for us?

00:26:09.336 --> 00:26:10.887
Yeah.

00:26:14.117 --> 00:26:17.828
Could always tell them the truth.

00:26:19.531 --> 00:26:20.741
Na...

00:26:20.776 --> 00:26:21.952
I know.

00:26:21.953 --> 00:26:25.029
I know, I know, I just...

00:26:25.064 --> 00:26:26.968
What's to become of these people?

00:26:27.003 --> 00:26:29.434
Sam, we only got one move
and you know it, all right?

00:26:29.469 --> 00:26:31.866
We got to wait for that Demon
to show itself and then...

00:26:31.901 --> 00:26:34.912
We get it before it gets them.

00:26:38.870 --> 00:26:41.962
I wonder what dad's doing.

00:26:43.831 --> 00:26:47.803
I would feel a lot better if
we were there backing him up.

00:26:50.090 --> 00:26:54.200
I would feel a lot better
if he was here backing us up.

00:28:30.162 --> 00:28:32.418
This is what we have.

00:28:32.920 --> 00:28:34.740
What?

00:28:35.260 --> 00:28:38.777
After all those years
we're finally here.

00:28:38.812 --> 00:28:41.430
It doesn't seem real.

00:28:42.303 --> 00:28:46.129
We just got to keep our heads
and do our job like always.

00:28:46.164 --> 00:28:49.460
Yeah, but this isn't like always.

00:28:52.241 --> 00:28:54.331
True.

00:28:55.947 --> 00:28:58.272
Dean, uh...

00:29:00.976 --> 00:29:03.418
I want to thank you.

00:29:04.473 --> 00:29:07.047
For what?

00:29:09.105 --> 00:29:11.643
For everything.

00:29:11.678 --> 00:29:13.852
You've always led my back you know.

00:29:13.887 --> 00:29:18.199
Even when I can't count on anyone
I could always count on you.

00:29:18.234 --> 00:29:20.288
And now...

00:29:20.643 --> 00:29:23.341
I don't know, I just
want to let you know.

00:29:23.376 --> 00:29:24.650
Just incase.

00:29:24.685 --> 00:29:27.115
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Are you kidding me?

00:29:27.150 --> 00:29:28.167
What?

00:29:28.202 --> 00:29:30.315
Don't say just incase
something happens to you.

00:29:30.350 --> 00:29:32.429
I don't want to hear
that freaking speech man.

00:29:32.464 --> 00:29:34.615
Nobody is dying tonight.

00:29:34.650 --> 00:29:37.723
Not us, not that family, nobody.

00:29:38.324 --> 00:29:40.575
Except that Demon.

00:29:40.610 --> 00:29:45.502
That evil son of a bitch ain't getting
any older than tonight. You understand me?

00:29:56.757 --> 00:29:58.949
John. You made it.

00:29:58.984 --> 00:30:01.106
Too bad really.

00:30:01.141 --> 00:30:03.569
I was hoping to kill
more of your friends.

00:30:03.604 --> 00:30:05.796
Sorry to disappoint.

00:30:05.831 --> 00:30:09.502
I can see where your
boys get their good looks.

00:30:09.537 --> 00:30:15.570
I must admit, considering what they
say about you I thought you'd be taller.

00:30:18.051 --> 00:30:20.823
Well, aren't you the chatty one?

00:30:20.858 --> 00:30:23.595
You want to get to business?

00:30:24.236 --> 00:30:25.939
Fine.

00:30:26.652 --> 00:30:28.591
Why don't you hand over the gun?

00:30:28.626 --> 00:30:31.593
If I give you the gun,
how do I get out of here?

00:30:31.628 --> 00:30:35.674
If you're as good as they say you are,
I'm sure you'll figure something out.

00:30:35.709 --> 00:30:37.618
Maybe I'll just shoot you.

00:30:37.653 --> 00:30:40.250
You want to shoot me, baby? Go ahead.

00:30:40.285 --> 00:30:45.327
It won't end anything.
There's more where I came from.

00:30:49.495 --> 00:30:51.061
Who the hell's that?

00:30:51.096 --> 00:30:55.435
He's not as nearly as much fun
as I am, I can tell you that.

00:30:55.470 --> 00:30:59.286
So, I suggest you give us the gun.

00:31:05.449 --> 00:31:07.786
Now!

00:31:18.044 --> 00:31:20.232
This is the Colt?

00:31:25.736 --> 00:31:28.272
What do you think?

00:31:49.569 --> 00:31:51.922
You shot me!

00:31:52.506 --> 00:31:56.089
I can't believe you just shot me!

00:31:57.321 --> 00:31:59.609
It's a fake!

00:32:09.475 --> 00:32:10.982
You're dead John.

00:32:11.017 --> 00:32:12.455
You're boys are dead.

00:32:12.490 --> 00:32:15.466
I never used the gun. How can
I know it would never work?

00:32:15.501 --> 00:32:18.443
I'm so not in the mood for
this. I've just been shot!

00:32:18.478 --> 00:32:21.371
Well I guess you're
lucky the gun wasn't real.

00:32:21.406 --> 00:32:23.164
That's funny, John.

00:32:23.199 --> 00:32:28.603
We're gonna strip the skin from
your bones but that was funny.

00:33:13.008 --> 00:33:15.561
Holy water, John.

00:33:15.596 --> 00:33:18.457
Real cute.

00:33:28.660 --> 00:33:31.241
Dad's not answering.

00:33:34.216 --> 00:33:36.133
Maybe Meg was late.

00:33:36.168 --> 00:33:37.756
Maybe the reception is bad.

00:33:37.791 --> 00:33:39.098
Yeah, well...

00:33:44.513 --> 00:33:46.715
Dean, wait.

00:33:47.599 --> 00:33:49.281
Listen.

00:34:12.309 --> 00:34:14.451
It's coming.

00:34:22.279 --> 00:34:23.832
Damn it.

00:34:51.769 --> 00:34:53.502
Get out of my house!

00:34:54.788 --> 00:34:56.522
Get out of my house!

00:34:58.482 --> 00:34:59.561
Mr. Hold, please.

00:34:59.596 --> 00:35:00.493
Be quite and listen to me.

00:35:00.494 --> 00:35:02.710
Be quite and listen to me.
We are trying to help you.

00:35:02.745 --> 00:35:03.714
Charlie?

00:35:03.749 --> 00:35:04.683
Okay?

00:35:04.684 --> 00:35:05.821
Everything okay down there?

00:35:05.856 --> 00:35:06.830
Monica, get the baby!

00:35:06.831 --> 00:35:08.007
Don't go over there!

00:35:08.042 --> 00:35:09.183
You stay away from her!

00:35:15.213 --> 00:35:17.559
What are you..

00:35:32.325 --> 00:35:33.758
Where the hell did it go?

00:35:33.793 --> 00:35:34.293
My baby!

00:35:34.328 --> 00:35:35.800
No, hey wait.

00:35:35.801 --> 00:35:37.740
Get her out of here, I got it.

00:35:38.010 --> 00:35:39.219
Come on.

00:35:39.254 --> 00:35:40.213
My baby!

00:35:40.248 --> 00:35:41.279
Dean's got her.

00:36:37.638 --> 00:36:39.623
You get away from my family!

00:36:39.658 --> 00:36:41.608
Charlie, don't. They saved us.

00:36:41.643 --> 00:36:43.255
They saved us...

00:36:51.130 --> 00:36:52.981
Thank you.

00:36:57.067 --> 00:36:58.733
It's still in there.

00:36:59.013 --> 00:37:00.128
Sam, Sam. No!

00:37:00.163 --> 00:37:01.504
Dean, let me go. It's still in there!

00:37:01.539 --> 00:37:02.845
It's burning to the
ground. It's suicide!

00:37:02.880 --> 00:37:03.714
I don't care!

00:37:03.749 --> 00:37:05.043
I do!

00:37:21.027 --> 00:37:24.889
Come on, dad. Answer
your phone, damn it!

00:37:28.494 --> 00:37:30.989
Something's wrong.

00:37:33.094 --> 00:37:35.266
You hear me? Something's happened.

00:37:35.301 --> 00:37:37.438
If you had just let me go in there...

00:37:37.473 --> 00:37:40.678
I could have ended all this.

00:37:40.713 --> 00:37:42.092
Sam...

00:37:42.127 --> 00:37:45.227
The only thing you
would end was your life.

00:37:45.905 --> 00:37:48.262
You don't know that.

00:37:48.297 --> 00:37:51.914
So what? You're willing to
sacrifice yourself? Is that it?

00:37:52.423 --> 00:37:54.665
Yeah. Yeah, you're damn right I am.

00:37:54.700 --> 00:37:56.907
Yeah, well that's not gonna
happen. Not as long as I'm around.

00:37:56.942 --> 00:37:58.451
What the hell are you
talking about Dean?

00:37:58.486 --> 00:38:01.217
We've been searching for
this Demon our whole lives.

00:38:01.252 --> 00:38:02.858
It's the only thing
we've ever cared about.

00:38:02.893 --> 00:38:05.667
Sam, I want to waste it. I do, okay?

00:38:05.702 --> 00:38:07.661
But it's not worth dying over?

00:38:07.696 --> 00:38:08.215
What?

00:38:08.250 --> 00:38:09.565
I mean it.

00:38:09.566 --> 00:38:13.035
If hunting this Demon means
you getting yourself killed.

00:38:13.070 --> 00:38:15.417
Then I hope we never
find the damn thing.

00:38:15.452 --> 00:38:18.433
That thing killed Jess.

00:38:19.335 --> 00:38:22.095
That thing killed mom.

00:38:22.563 --> 00:38:25.478
You said yourself once.

00:38:25.629 --> 00:38:28.621
That no matter what we do they're gone

00:38:28.656 --> 00:38:31.063
and they're never coming back.

00:38:31.521 --> 00:38:34.284
Don't just say that! Don't you!

00:38:34.319 --> 00:38:37.047
After all this, don't you say that.

00:38:38.629 --> 00:38:42.230
Sam, look.

00:38:42.265 --> 00:38:45.082
The three of us...

00:38:45.285 --> 00:38:48.081
That's all we have.

00:38:49.587 --> 00:38:52.611
It's all I have.

00:38:55.834 --> 00:39:00.092
Sometimes I feel like I'm
barely holding it together, man.

00:39:00.954 --> 00:39:03.846
Without you and dad...

00:39:04.820 --> 00:39:06.889
Dad...

00:39:11.975 --> 00:39:14.351
He should have called by now.

00:39:14.386 --> 00:39:16.851
Try again.

00:39:33.377 --> 00:39:37.189
You boys really screwed up this time.

00:39:40.058 --> 00:39:42.408
Where is he?

00:39:42.588 --> 00:39:45.840
You're never gonna
see your father again.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
